ID is a file path inside ~/.config (hypr/bindings.conf), an app directory (hypr),
a tracked file (~/.gitconfig), a package or unit name, or a group: packages, services.
No ID means all changes.

$ syschange version
0.3.1

$ syschange nope
error: unknown command "nope", see syschange help

$ syschange status --bogus
error: flag provided but not defined: -bogus

$ syschange init
Tracking <tmp>/001/config. History lives in <tmp>/001/state.

$ syschange status
Nothing new. Everything is recorded.

$ syschange status --json
{"initialized":true,"count":0,"pending":null,"history":null,"configDir":"<tmp>/001/config","agents":[],"checkpoints":[],"autoExport":"","version":"0.3.1"}

$ syschange status
Hyprland  [hypr]
  ~ Key bindings  +1 -1
Kitty  [kitty]
  + kitty.conf  +1 -0
Waybar  [waybar]
  + config  +1 -0

Record with: syschange note "why" [ID...]   undo with: syschange revert ID...

