$ syschange track

$ syschange export --to <tmp>/007/out.md
Exported to <tmp>/007/out.md.

$ syschange export --auto <tmp>/002/auto.md
Exported to <tmp>/002/auto.md, and it will be kept up to date.

$ syschange export --auto off
Auto export is off.

$ syschange export --auto <tmp>/001/config/x.md
error: <tmp>/001/config/x.md is inside <tmp>/001/config, which syschange tracks: pick a file elsewhere

$ syschange remote
No backup remote. Set one: syschange remote set URL

$ syschange push
error: no backup remote, set one with: syschange remote set URL

$ syschange remote bogus
error: usage: syschange remote [set URL | off]

$ syschange remote set <tmp>/004/b.git
Backed up to <tmp>/004/b.git. Every change is pushed from now on.
Keep that repository private: it holds your config files.

$ syschange remote
<tmp>/004/b.git
last push <time>: ok

$ syschange push
Pushed to <tmp>/004/b.git.

$ syschange push --quiet

$ syschange remote off
Backup is off. The remote keeps what it has.

$ syschange apply
error: usage: syschange apply [--yes] URL-or-path-of-a-backup

$ syschange apply <tmp>/004/b.git
From <tmp>/004/b.git:
  nothing to do, this machine already matches (3 files identical)

$ syschange apply <tmp>/005/o.git
From <tmp>/005/o.git:
  overwrite ~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf
  add       ~/.config/mpv/mpv.conf
error: run with --yes to apply

$ syschange apply --yes <tmp>/005/o.git
From <tmp>/005/o.git:
  overwrite ~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf
  add       ~/.config/mpv/mpv.conf
Applied. Undo the config part with: syschange restore "Before applying <tmp>/005/o.git"

$ syschange hook
error: usage: syschange hook claude|codex|gemini|grok [start]

$ syschange hook cursor
error: usage: syschange hook claude|codex|gemini|grok [start]

$ syschange hook claude start

$ syschange hook claude start

$ syschange hook claude pre

$ syschange hook claude post

$ syschange hook claude
{"decision":"block","reason":"You changed this system during the session. Before finishing, record why, one short line per logical change:\n- modified hypr/bindings.conf (Key bindings)\n\nRun: syschange note --by claude \"\u003cwhy, in the user's language\u003e\" \u003cid\u003e...\nIf one of these is not yours, leave it out. To keep a path out of the history for good: syschange ignore \u003cpath\u003e."}

$ syschange hook omarchy theme-set x

$ syschange agents
No supported agent found (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI or Grok).

$ syschange agents install
error: no supported agent found (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI or Grok)

$ syschange agents status
claude (Omarchy default): not connected, run: syschange agents install

$ syschange agents install claude
Connected: claude. Agents now describe the system changes they make.

